    "recommendations": "• Mark the single driveway entrance with reflective address numbers visible from both directions on the road.\n• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entry that is visible at night and in low-visibility conditions.\n• Keep a gate or pathway on at least one side of the property unlocked and clear to allow responders to reach the rear without passing through the main structure.\n• Trim dense vegetation along the sides of the property to create a walking path wide enough for responders carrying equipment.\n• Cut back any dense vegetation that overhangs or narrows the path between the detached structures and the main building.\n• Mark the locations of both detached structures on any posted property map or address placard so responders arriving for the first time can quickly account for all buildings.\n• Keep the area around the water feature clear of dense vegetation so responders can identify and avoid it quickly during low-light or high-stress operations.\n• Post a simple site map near the main entrance showing the location of all structures, the water feature, and any side access points.\n• Clear a staging area in the vehicle parking zone wide enough for at least one emergency vehicle to park without blocking the single access point.\n• Trim vegetation along the perimeter fence line so responders can move around the inside of the fence without obstruction."
